# The runtime exclude list: what the release tarball carries and what stays out (Estadística's).
#
# pack-app.sh (the org's shared app-release workflow) reads this file with rsync rules anchored
# at the app root, and it REPLACES the packer's defaults, so it lists every development path
# itself; '!' re-include lines are refused. The tarball carries appinfo/, js/ (built by the
# release), lib/, seeds/ (the shipped data), templates/, img/, vendor/aps/common/src (aps-common,
# committed), LICENSE and README.md: an install needs no build step. vendor/ needs no rule: the release packs a fresh
# checkout, which holds only what git tracks under it.
# /.* covers every dotfile and dot directory at the root, this file and .htaccess included.
- /.*
- /src
- /tests
- /docs
- /scripts
- /tools
- /CHANGELOG.md
- /openapi.json
- /AGENTS.md
- /CONTEXT.md
- /Makefile
- /package.json
- /package-lock.json
- /composer.json
- /composer.lock
- /phpunit.xml
- /phpunit.seam.xml
- /eslint.config.mjs
- /webpack.config.js
- /Dockerfile.test
- /compose.dev.yaml
# Sourcemaps name every source path of the build machine.
- /js/*.map
